<title>NORWAY: Statoil in oil deal with Ireland's INPC.</title>
<headline>Statoil in oil deal with Ireland's INPC.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) said on Thursday it had signed an agreement to deliver an initial 700,000 tonnes per year of crude to the Whitegate refinery in Cork under a processing deal with Irish state oil company INPC.</p>
<p>A Statoil spokesman said the oil was light North Sea crude, primarily Oseberg. The first cargo of 600,000 barrels is due to be delivered on Friday, he said.</p>
<p>The agreement covers about 25 percent of the plant's capacity, but the volume could be increased, Statoil said.</p>
<p>The state Norwegian oil company said the deal ensure stable deliveries for Statoil Ireland, which has around 350 service stations in the Irish Republic.</p>
<p>-- Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
